		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>VLOOKUP is the most used lookup function in Excel. This guide covers it from zero to hero with real examples.</p>
<p>For the basics read the <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/excel">official docs</a> first.</p>
<h2>Exact match vs approximate</h2>
<ul>
<li>FALSE means exact match</li>
<li>TRUE means approximate</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>Master VLOOKUP and you master half of Excel.</blockquote>
<figure><img src="http://127.0.0.1:8765/img2.png" alt="Growth chart" srcset="http://127.0.0.1:8765/img2-300x180.png 300w, http://127.0.0.1:8765/img2.png 800w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" /><figcaption>Sample chart</figcaption></figure>
<script>alert('this must be dropped')</script>
<style>.wp-block-x{display:none}</style>
<p>Practice with the sample workbook below.</p>]]></content:encoded>
